  "id": "gamma-synchrony",
  "term": "gamma synchrony",
  "definition": "Gamma synchrony is the matching or coordination of brain activity in the gamma frequency range across cortical signals, measured here as phase synchrony. In this study, stronger gamma synchrony was found in dancers while listening to music compared with silence or silent dance.",
